  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ef868150",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Dummy показывает базовый уровень. Все остальные модели должны значительно её превзойти."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5c19156b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Обучите несколько архитектур линейных моделей. Они могут различаться по ряду черт: набором отобранных признаков, масштабом признаков, установленными гиперпараметрами, функциями потерь. Попробуйте обучить следующие модели:\n",
    "\n",
    "LinearRegression;\n",
    "Lasso (L1-регуляризация);\n",
    "Ridge (L2-регуляризация);\n",
    "SGDRegressor.\n",
    "Обязательно попробуйте модели с разными значениями гиперпараметра loss."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 57,
   "id": "14d10bdd",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "models = {\n",
    "    \"LinearRegression\": LinearRegression(),\n",
    "    \"Ridge\":            Ridge(alpha=1.0),\n",
    "    \"Lasso\":            Lasso(alpha=1.0),\n",
    "    \"SGD_squared_loss\": SGDRegressor(loss='squared_loss', max_iter=1000, random_state=42, learning_rate='adaptive'),\n",
    "    \"SGD_epsilon_insensitive\": SGDRegressor(loss='epsilon_insensitive', max_iter=1000, random_state=42, learning_rate='adaptive')\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "datasets = {\n",
    "    \"raw\":  (X_train_raw, X_valid_raw),\n",
    "    \"std\":  (X_train_std, X_valid_std),\n",
    "    \"norm\": (X_train_norm, X_valid_norm)\n",
    "}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 58,
   "id": "94591990",
   "metadata": {
    "scrolled": true
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# RAW\n",
    "for name, model in models.items():\n",
    "    model.fit(X_train_raw, y_train)\n",
    "    y_pred = model.predict(X_valid_raw)\n",
    "    metrics = get_metrics(y_valid, y_pred, f\"{name}\")\n",
    "    results.append(metrics)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 59,
   "id": "f26f216d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#STD\n",
    "for name, model in models.items():\n",
    "    model.fit(X_train_std, y_train)\n",
    "    y_pred = model.predict(X_valid_std)\n",
    "    metrics = get_metrics(y_valid, y_pred, f\"{name}\")\n",
    "    results.append(metrics)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 60,
   "id": "5ad65469",
   "metadata": {
    "scrolled": true
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#NORM\n",
    "for name, model in models.items():\n",
    "    model.fit(X_train_norm, y_train)\n",
    "    y_pred = model.predict(X_valid_norm)\n",
    "    metrics = get_metrics(y_valid, y_pred, f\"{name}\")\n",
    "    results.append(metrics)"
   ]
  },
  {
